old_sentence:
\section{Historical development of the theories reviewed}\label{sec:history}
\subsection{A short history}
\paragraph{Origins (1830s--1950s).} Duhamel's memoir of 1837 \citep{Duhamel1837} established the stress--strain--temperature relation that still bears his name (with Neumann's later contribution): the stress depends on strain and on the temperature increment through an expansion coefficient.

